<title>FINLAND: FINNS LEAST KEEN ON EMU IN EU POLL - PAPER.</title>
<headline>FINNS LEAST KEEN ON EMU IN EU POLL - PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Support for Europe's planned single currency is lower in Finland than any other European Union country, according to a &quot;eurobarometer&quot; poll by the European Commission, daily Helsingin Sanomat said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said only 29 percent of Finns support economic and monetary union (EMU) with 56 percent against, showing a table where British support was second from bottom with 31 percent for, 57 percent against.</p>
<p>Support was the highest in Italy: 73 percent for and 11 percent against. The paper said the survey had been carried out last October-November among 31,800 people in EU member states.</p>
<p>It did not detail the questions asked.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
